IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 9 GENERAL PROVISIONS: s 93 (exclusion of liability of public telecommunication licensees), s 94 (service of documents), s 97 (regulations).
-- (ss 95, 96 and 98 are in sgta-part9-general.l4.)
-- 2000 Revised Edition number of s 97 is s 74; the subsidiary instruments cite it under that number.

§ `s 93 Exclusion of liability of public telecommunication licensees`

-- src:6809 | 93. A public telecommunication licensee is not liable in respect of
-- src:6810 | any injury, loss or damage suffered by any person by reason of —
-- src:6812 | (a) any failure to provide or delay in providing any
-- src:6813 | telecommunication services or any equipment associated
-- src:6814 | therewith or service ancillary thereto;
-- src:6816 | (b) any failure, interruption, suspension or restriction of any
-- src:6817 | telecommunication service or service ancillary thereto or
-- src:6818 | delay of, or fault in, any communication by means of
-- src:6819 | telecommunications;
-- src:6821 | (c) any error in, or omission of, any information transmitted
-- src:6822 | through telecommunications; or
-- src:6824 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6825 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 138
-- src:6827 | (d) any loss of secrecy in communication arising from the use
-- src:6828 | of any telecommunication service,
-- src:6830 | which is due to the act or default of another person, or an accident or
-- src:6831 | some other cause beyond the public telecommunication licensee’s
-- src:6832 | control.
@ref s 93 (src:6809-6832)
GIVEN `the injury, loss or damage is by reason of a failure to provide, or delay in providing, a telecommunication service or associated equipment or ancillary service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury, loss or damage is by reason of a failure, interruption, suspension or restriction of a telecommunication service or ancillary service, or a delay of, or fault in, a communication by means of telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury, loss or damage is by reason of an error in, or omission of, information transmitted through telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury, loss or damage is by reason of a loss of secrecy in communication arising from the use of a telecommunication service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is due to the act or default of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is due to an accident or some other cause beyond the licensee's control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 93: the public telecommunication licensee is liable for the injury, loss or damage` MEANS
    NOT (    (   `the injury, loss or damage is by reason of a failure to provide, or delay in providing, a telecommunication service or associated equipment or ancillary service`
              OR `the injury, loss or damage is by reason of a failure, interruption, suspension or restriction of a telecommunication service or ancillary service, or a delay of, or fault in, a communication by means of telecommunications`
              OR `the injury, loss or damage is by reason of an error in, or omission of, information transmitted through telecommunications`
              OR `the injury, loss or damage is by reason of a loss of secrecy in communication arising from the use of a telecommunication service`)
         AND (`it is due to the act or default of another person` OR `it is due to an accident or some other cause beyond the licensee's control`))

§ `s 94 Service of documents, etc.`

-- src:6838 | 94.—(1) Subject to subsection (6), any decision, notice, order or
-- src:6839 | document required or authorised to be given by the Authority, or
-- src:6840 | served by the Authority on any person, under this Act, or under any
-- src:6841 | code of practice or standard of performance, may be served —
-- src:6843 | (a) in the case of an individual —
-- src:6845 | (i) by delivering the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6846 | to the individual personally;
-- src:6848 | (ii) by leaving the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6849 | with an adult person apparently resident at the usual
-- src:6850 | or last known address of the place of residence of the
-- src:6851 | individual;
-- src:6853 | (iii) by leaving the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6854 | with an adult person apparently employed at the
-- src:6855 | usual or last known address of the place of business
-- src:6856 | of the individual;
-- src:6858 | (iv) by affixing the decision, notice, order or document in
-- src:6859 | a conspicuous place at the usual or last known
-- src:6860 | address of the place of residence or business of the
-- src:6861 | individual;
-- src:6863 | (v) by sending the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6864 | by prepaid registered post addressed to the individual
-- src:6865 | at the usual or last known address of the place of
-- src:6866 | residence or business of the individual;
-- src:6868 | (vi) by sending the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6869 | by fax transmission to the last fax transmission
-- src:6870 | number of the individual given to the Authority by
-- src:6871 | the individual; or
-- src:6873 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6874 | 139 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:6876 | (vii) by sending an electronic communication of the
-- src:6877 | decision, notice, order or document to the last
-- src:6878 | electronic mail address of the individual given to
-- src:6879 | the Authority by the individual;
-- src:6881 | (b) in the case of a partnership other than a limited liability
-- src:6882 | partnership —
-- src:6884 | (i) by delivering the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6885 | to any one of the partners or the secretary or other
-- src:6886 | like officer of the partnership;
-- src:6888 | (ii) by leaving the decision, notice, order or document at,
-- src:6889 | or by sending the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6890 | by prepaid registered post to, the principal or last
-- src:6891 | known place of business of the partnership in
-- src:6892 | Singapore;
-- src:6894 | (iii) by sending the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6895 | by fax transmission to the last fax transmission
-- src:6896 | number of the partnership given to the Authority by
-- src:6897 | the partnership; or
-- src:6899 | (iv) by sending an electronic communication of the
-- src:6900 | decision, notice, order or document to the last
-- src:6901 | electronic mail address of the partnership given to
-- src:6902 | the Authority by the partnership; and
-- src:6904 | (c) in the case of a limited liability partnership or any other
-- src:6905 | body corporate —
-- src:6907 | (i) by delivering the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6908 | to the manager of the limited liability partnership or
-- src:6909 | the secretary or other like officer of the body
-- src:6910 | corporate;
-- src:6912 | (ii) by leaving the decision, notice, order or document at,
-- src:6913 | or by sending the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6914 | by prepaid registered post to, the registered office or
-- src:6915 | principal office of the limited liability partnership or
-- src:6916 | body corporate in Singapore;
-- src:6918 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6919 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 140
-- src:6921 | (iii) by sending the decision, notice, order or document
-- src:6922 | by fax transmission to the last fax transmission
-- src:6923 | number of the limited liability partnership or body
-- src:6924 | corporate given to the Authority by the limited
-- src:6925 | liability partnership or body corporate; or
-- src:6927 | (iv) by sending an electronic communication of the
-- src:6928 | decision, notice, order or document to the last
-- src:6929 | electronic mail address of the limited liability
-- src:6930 | partnership or body corporate given to the
-- src:6931 | Authority by the limited liability partnership or
-- src:6932 | body corporate.
-- src:6934 | [19/2011]
@ref s 94(1) (src:6838-6934)
GIVEN `it is not a notice or document to be served in proceedings in court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person served is an individual, a partnership other than a limited liability partnership, or a limited liability partnership or other body corporate` IS A STRING
      method IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 94(1): the Authority may serve the decision, notice, order or document on the person by this method` MEANS
    `it is not a notice or document to be served in proceedings in court`
    AND BRANCH IF `the person served is an individual, a partnership other than a limited liability partnership, or a limited liability partnership or other body corporate` EQUALS "individual"
                 THEN elem method (LIST "delivering it to the individual personally"
                                      , "leaving it with an adult person apparently resident at the usual or last known address of the place of residence of the individual"
                                      , "leaving it with an adult person apparently employed at the usual or last known address of the place of business of the individual"
                                      , "affixing it in a conspicuous place at the usual or last known address of the place of residence or business of the individual"
                                      , "sending it by prepaid registered post addressed to the individual at the usual or last known address of residence or business"
                                      , "sending it by fax transmission to the last fax transmission number of the individual given to the Authority"
                                      , "sending an electronic communication of it to the last electronic mail address of the individual given to the Authority")
               IF `the person served is an individual, a partnership other than a limited liability partnership, or a limited liability partnership or other body corporate` EQUALS "partnership"
                 THEN elem method (LIST "delivering it to any one of the partners or the secretary or other like officer of the partnership"
                                      , "leaving it at, or sending it by prepaid registered post to, the principal or last known place of business of the partnership in Singapore"
                                      , "sending it by fax transmission to the last fax transmission number of the partnership given to the Authority"
                                      , "sending an electronic communication of it to the last electronic mail address of the partnership given to the Authority")
               OTHERWISE elem method (LIST "delivering it to the manager of the limited liability partnership or the secretary or other like officer of the body corporate"
                                          , "leaving it at, or sending it by prepaid registered post to, the registered office or principal office of the limited liability partnership or body corporate in Singapore"
                                          , "sending it by fax transmission to the last fax transmission number of the limited liability partnership or body corporate given to the Authority"
                                          , "sending an electronic communication of it to the last electronic mail address of the limited liability partnership or body corporate given to the Authority")

-- src:6936 | (2) Where any decision, notice, order or other document required or
-- src:6937 | authorised to be given by the Authority, or served by the Authority on
-- src:6938 | any person, under this Act is sent by prepaid registered post, the
-- src:6939 | decision, notice, order or document is deemed to have been duly
-- src:6940 | served on the person to whom it is addressed 2 days after the day it
-- src:6941 | was posted, whether or not it is returned undelivered.
@ref s 94(2) (src:6936-6941)
GIVEN `days after the day it was posted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 94(2): the document sent by prepaid registered post is deemed duly served, whether or not it is returned undelivered` MEANS
    `days after the day it was posted` AT LEAST 2

-- src:6945 | (3) Where any decision, notice, order or other document required or
-- src:6946 | authorised to be given by the Authority, or served by the Authority on
-- src:6947 | any person, under this Act is sent by fax transmission to a fax
-- src:6948 | transmission number in accordance with subsection (1), the decision,
-- src:6949 | notice, order or document is deemed to have been duly served on the
-- src:6950 | person to whom it is addressed on the day of the transmission, subject
-- src:6951 | to the receipt on the sending fax machine of a notification (by
-- src:6952 | electronic or other means) of a successful transmission to the fax
-- src:6953 | machine for that fax transmission number.
@ref s 94(3) (src:6945-6953)
GIVEN `it is the day of the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification of successful transmission was received on the sending fax machine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 94(3): the document sent by fax transmission is deemed duly served` MEANS
    `it is the day of the transmission` AND `a notification of successful transmission was received on the sending fax machine`

-- src:6957 | (4) Where any decision, notice, order or other document required or
-- src:6958 | authorised to be given by the Authority, or served by the Authority on
-- src:6959 | any person, under this Act is sent by electronic communication to an
-- src:6960 | electronic mail address in accordance with subsection (1), the
-- src:6961 | decision, notice, order or document is deemed to have been duly
-- src:6962 | served on the person to whom it is addressed at the time the electronic
-- src:6963 | communication enters the information system for that electronic mail
-- src:6964 | address.
@ref s 94(4) (src:6957-6964)
GIVEN `the electronic communication has entered the information system for the electronic mail address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 94(4): the document sent by electronic communication is deemed duly served` MEANS
    `the electronic communication has entered the information system for the electronic mail address`

-- src:6971 | (5) Service of any decision, notice, order or other document under
-- src:6972 | this Act may be effected on a person by electronic communication
-- src:6973 | only if the person gives as part of the person’s address for service an
-- src:6974 | electronic mail address.
@ref s 94(5) (src:6971-6974)
GIVEN `the person gives, as part of the person's address for service, an electronic mail address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 94(5): service may be effected on the person by electronic communication` MEANS
    `the person gives, as part of the person's address for service, an electronic mail address`

-- src:6978 | (6) This section does not apply to notices and documents to be
-- src:6979 | served in proceedings in court.
@ref s 94(6) (src:6978-6979)
GIVEN `the notice or document is to be served in proceedings in court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 94(6): section 94 applies to the notice or document` MEANS
    NOT `the notice or document is to be served in proceedings in court`

§ `s 97 Regulations`

-- src:7007 | 97.—(1) The Authority may, with the approval of the Minister,
-- src:7008 | make regulations for any purpose for which regulations are required
-- src:7009 | to be made under this Act and generally for carrying out the purposes
-- src:7010 | and provisions of this Act.
@ref s 97(1) (src:7007-7010)
GIVEN `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations are for a purpose for which regulations are required to be made under the Act, or generally for carrying out its purposes and provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(1): the Authority may make the regulations` MEANS
    `the Minister approved` AND `the regulations are for a purpose for which regulations are required to be made under the Act, or generally for carrying out its purposes and provisions`

-- src:7012 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Authority may, with the
-- src:7013 | approval of the Minister, make regulations for or with respect to all or
-- src:7014 | any of the following matters:
-- src:7016 | (a) the proficiency examinations, including the syllabi and the
-- src:7017 | details of such examinations, for the certification of
-- src:7018 | competency of individuals operating telecommunication
-- src:7019 | services or for the grant of any licence by the Authority;
-- src:7021 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:7022 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 142
-- src:7024 | (b) the classes and the conditions for the grant of licences and
-- src:7025 | spectrum rights by the Authority;
-- src:7027 | (c) in relation to cable detection work licences —
-- src:7029 | (i) the class or classes of licences to be granted, the form
-- src:7030 | and duration of those licences, the terms and
-- src:7031 | conditions upon, and the circumstances in, which
-- src:7032 | those licences may be granted, held, suspended,
-- src:7033 | cancelled, altered, extended, renewed or replaced
-- src:7034 | and the fees payable in respect thereof;
-- src:7036 | (ii) the qualifications and other requirements for
-- src:7037 | applicants for such licences, the examination or
-- src:7038 | testing of such applicants, the fees payable in respect
-- src:7039 | of such examination or testing and the circumstances
-- src:7040 | in and conditions on which an applicant may be
-- src:7041 | exempted from such examination or testing; and
-- src:7043 | (iii) the duties and responsibilities of licensed cable
-- src:7044 | detection workers;
-- src:7046 | (d) the control and regulation of dealing in and use of
-- src:7047 | telecommunication equipment;
-- src:7049 | (e) the control and regulation of interference by radiowaves or
-- src:7050 | electrical or other means to telecommunications in
-- src:7051 | Singapore;
-- src:7053 | (f) the control and regulation of installation, wiring, cabling
-- src:7054 | and other types of works to be carried out on the
-- src:7055 | telecommunication systems of a telecommunication
-- src:7056 | system licensee;
-- src:7058 | (g) the control and regulation of the allocation and use of —
-- src:7060 | (i) telephone numbers; and
-- src:7062 | (ii) any other numbers used for or in connection with
-- src:7063 | either or both of the following:
-- src:7065 | (A) the operation of telecommunication systems;
-- src:7067 | (B) the provision of telecommunication services;
-- src:7069 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:7070 | 143 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:7072 | (ga) the prescribing of any rate of interest for any provision of
-- src:7073 | this Act, which may be by way of formula or other method,
-- src:7074 | and which may incorporate by reference any formula or
-- src:7075 | method of another body or organisation, as may be
-- src:7076 | amended from time to time;
-- src:7078 | [Act 13 of 2026 wef 02/10/2026]
-- src:7080 | (h) the prescribing of anything that is required or permitted to
-- src:7081 | be prescribed under this Act.
-- src:7082 | [74
-- src:7084 | [10/2005; 19/2011; 30/2016]
@ref s 97(2) (src:7012-7084)
GIVEN matter IS A STRING
      `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(2): the Authority may make regulations for or with respect to this matter` MEANS
    `the Minister approved`
    AND elem matter (LIST "the proficiency examinations, including the syllabi and the details, for the certification of competency of individuals operating telecommunication services or for the grant of a licence by the Authority"
                         , "the classes and the conditions for the grant of licences and spectrum rights by the Authority"
                         , "cable detection work licences: the classes, form and duration, the terms and conditions and circumstances of grant, holding, suspension, cancellation, alteration, extension, renewal or replacement, and the fees"
                         , "cable detection work licences: the qualifications and other requirements for applicants, the examination or testing and its fees, and the circumstances and conditions of exemption from it"
                         , "cable detection work licences: the duties and responsibilities of licensed cable detection workers"
                         , "the control and regulation of dealing in and use of telecommunication equipment"
                         , "the control and regulation of interference by radiowaves or electrical or other means to telecommunications in Singapore"
                         , "the control and regulation of installation, wiring, cabling and other types of works to be carried out on the telecommunication systems of a telecommunication system licensee"
                         , "the control and regulation of the allocation and use of telephone numbers"
                         , "the control and regulation of the allocation and use of any other numbers used for or in connection with the operation of telecommunication systems or the provision of telecommunication services"
                         , "the prescribing of any rate of interest for any provision of the Act, by formula or other method, which may incorporate by reference any formula or method of another body or organisation as amended from time to time"
                         , "the prescribing of anything that is required or permitted to be prescribed under the Act")
